From bf8238ecc5ee19f2e0f1d6ed2a2c7c8e3f3a8bdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:53:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(plugins,kanban): a slow pre_tool_call guard no
 longer refuses a worker's park/report calls or books the run a protocol
 violation

2026-11-12 laptop-1: one `_pre_tool_call` callback timed out; for the next 60 s core refused every tool
call (fail-closed + suppression), kanban_continue/kanban_comment/kanban_heartbeat included, with a message
naming neither the plugin nor when to retry. The worker ended its turn rc=0 and the dispatcher booked a
protocol violation (counted, failure notice). Two runs of t_01a1ce9070eee14c were lost.

1. plugins_dispatch: when a fail-closed pre_tool_call callback is skipped (suppressed, still running,
   abandoned-worker cap, timed out, worker failed to start), kanban_block / kanban_continue /
   kanban_schedule / kanban_heartbeat / kanban_comment / kanban_request_review get no block directive:
   the tool runs and ONE WARNING names the skipped callback. kanban_complete and every other tool stay
   fail-closed. Same on the async path.
2. The timed-out / skipped / finished-late / abandoned-cap / start-failure WARNINGs and the refusal text
   the agent sees name the callback's module (cb.__module__); a suppression refusal says "retry in N s".
3. kanban_guard_refusal (dead-worker sweep): a clean exit whose last 6 tool results (its registered
   worker session in state.db) include that refusal on a kanban_* call is rebooked like an owner-restart
   loss: requeued, no failure counted, no failure notice, run metadata `guard_refusal`. Bounded: after 3
   such consecutive runs the next is charged as a protocol violation again.

Card: t_01a1d0d8dbf676af
